3.	A DNS assessment report generated using the Dig tool shows that the organization&#39;s DNS server permits a successful DNS Zone Transfer (AXFR), exposing internal hostnames, mail servers, and DNS records. Analyze the report and explain the security implications of the exposed information. Discuss how attackers could exploit these findings and recommend best practices to secure the DNS infrastructure. (10 Marks)

# Query DNS records
dig example.com

# Query A record
dig example.com A

# Query MX (Mail Exchange) records
dig example.com MX

# Query NS (Name Server) records
dig example.com NS

# Query SOA (Start of Authority) record
dig example.com SOA

# Attempt a DNS Zone Transfer (AXFR)
dig @192.168.1.10 example.com AXFR

# Attempt a DNS Zone Transfer using the DNS server hostname
dig @ns1.example.com example.com AXFR

# Perform a reverse DNS lookup
dig -x 192.168.1.10

# Display all DNS information
dig example.com ANY
